### What did you do?

<details>
<summary>Configuration</summary>

```js
import { defineConfig, globalIgnores } from "eslint/config";
import nextVitals from "eslint-config-next/core-web-vitals";
import nextTs from "eslint-config-next/typescript";

const eslintConfig = defineConfig([
  ...nextVitals,
  ...nextTs,
  // Override default ignores of eslint-config-next.
  globalIgnores([
    // Default ignores of eslint-config-next:
    ".next/**",
    "out/**",
    "build/**",
    "next-env.d.ts",
  ]),
]);

export default eslintConfig;

```
</details>

An `eslint(react-hooks/set-state-in-effect)` error is raised from the below code.
```js
    const [state, setState] = useState(1);
    const updateState = () => {
        setState(2);
    }
    useEffect(() => {
        updateState();
    },[])
```
But no linting error is raised from the below code
```js
    const [state, setState] = useState(1);
    useEffect(() => {
        const updateState = () => {
            setState(2);
        }
        updateState();
    },[])
```


### What did you expect to happen?

I expect the error to be raised in both cases

### What actually happened?

The error is only raised when the function performing the `setState()` is not inside the `useEffect()`

