### Additional comments

This appears to specifically affect reads inside parameter decorator expressions and reproduces in the official ESLint playground using `@typescript-eslint/parser` with no external framework dependencies.

Equivalent patterns using class decorators or method decorators do not reproduce the issue.

This pattern is commonly used in frameworks like NestJS:
```ts
@Body(validationPipe)
```
where module-level pipe instances are passed into parameter decorators.

